# .trivyignore — Trivy CVE snooze list
#
# Format: CVE-YYYY-NNNNN  # snooze: expires YYYY-MM-DD  reason: <brief explanation>
#
# Rules:
#   1. Every entry MUST include an "expires YYYY-MM-DD" comment.
#      Entries without an expiry are rejected by the CI snooze-verify step.
#   2. Expiry date should not exceed 90 days from the snooze date.
#   3. Renewing a snooze requires a fresh PR with an updated expiry and
#      a comment explaining why the vulnerability is still acceptable.
#
# Example (do not uncomment unless the CVE is confirmed as a false positive):
#
# CVE-2024-12345  # snooze: expires 2026-10-31  reason: only affects musl libc, image uses glibc
